<title>SOUTH KOREA: Samsung up on jet trainer programme.</title>
<headline>Samsung up on jet trainer programme.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Samsung Aerospace Industries Co rose to their daily limit in late Friday morning on the government's decision to develop advanced jet trainer aircraft, brokers said.</p>
<p>Samsung Aerospace shares were up eight percent, or 800 won, to 10,800 won and trading volume was a high 273,670 shares.  </p>
<p>The defence ministry said on Thursday the development programme would start in the second half of 1997 for completion in 2005. The aircraft would initially be delivered to the Korean Air Force in late 2005.</p>
<p>&quot;Samsung Aerospace shares are also attractive when investors are focusing on medium- to low-end stocks,&quot; said Koh Soon-shik of LG Securities.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
